    "question": {
      ":question/id": "c399cb95-bcb5-55c0-a42d-ed9fc4042cb6",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following augmented matrices have coefficient matrices that are **not** in row echelon form? Treat the final column of each augmented matrix as its constants column.\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "A coefficient matrix, obtained by omitting the final column of its augmented matrix, is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\nI. All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n\nII. Each leading entry of a nonzero row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the preceding nonzero row.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The coefficient matrix of $A$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}11 & -6 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The coefficient matrix of $B$ is not in row echelon form since the leading entry in row $2$, column $3$ is in the same column as the leading entry in row $1$, column $3$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nB=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 0 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8 & -9\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The coefficient matrix of $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}-2 & 7 & -2 & -2 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 10 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 8 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nTherefore, select $B$.",
